ALL THAT CERTAIN tract or parcel of land and premises situate, lying and being in the Borough of HADDONFIELD, County of CAMDEN and State of New Jersey more particularly described as follows:

BEGINNING at a point in the Southeasterly line of Kings Highway East, as approved December 15, 1931 and adopted by Ordinance February 16, 1932 by Borough Commissioners, 171.76 feet Northeasterly from the Easterly corner of Kings Highway East and Chestnut Street, said beginning point being corner to remaining lands of George H. Heacock and Dorothy H. Heacock;

THENCE: Northeasterly along Southeasterly line of Kings Highway East, 84 feet to point corner to lands of Trustees of Baptist Church of Haddonfield (formerly John Clement) and said point also being 97.23 feet Southeasterly from westerly wall of 123 Kings Highway East; and

THENCE: Southeasterly forming interior angle of 89°46'45" with Kings Highway East and running along lands of said Trustees of Baptist Church of Haddonfield 231.84 feet to point in line of said Trustees of Baptist Church and corner to lands of the Borough of Haddonfield;

THENCE: Southwesterly along lands of Borough of Haddonfield and forming an interior angle of 89°44'10" with the last course 83.05 feet to point corner of remaining lands of Estate of Charles H. Hill; and also along line of remaining lands of George H. Heacock and Dorothy H. Heacock aforesaid and forming an interior angle of 90°30' with last course and also forming an interior angle of 89°59'5" with Kings Highway East 83.15 feet to Southeasterly line of Kings Highway East and place of beginning.

BEING KNOWN as Lot 6, Block 34, as shown on the tax map of the Borough of Haddonfield. (For information only)
